An high level example would be considering nodal strength. One could start off by using just the DMN nodes to construct the graph and obtain nodal strength measures, then later expand the graph to include all other nodes outside DMN and recalculate nodal strength again. This could provide insights regarding the level of contributions originating from outside the DMN network.

Does this make sense?

Sean

